 > `VICTORY_D3D12_WARP=1`, which renders on the software adapter.
 
 `VICTORY_RECOVER_REMOVAL=1` opts into forensic capture (default off).
+Before device creation this selects DRED page-fault tracking with
+AutoBreadcrumbs explicitly **off**. Allocation/object lifetime tracking and
+object names still cost CPU/memory at creation/destruction. Per-command notes,
+markers and AutoBreadcrumb metadata/progress recording are disabled by default.
+`VICTORY_RECOVER_REMOVAL_BREADCRUMBS=1` separately opts into that recurring
+command-list/allocation/submission cost, including ExecuteCommandLists tracking.
+The diagnostics `VICTORY_D3D12_DRED` flag cannot bypass this recovery sub-flag.
+Without breadcrumbs, pending command count is unavailable (`null`). No title
+CPU/frame-time delta has been measured for either mode.
+
 After removal, a separate instance of this executable suspends every title
 process thread except a dedicated termination watchdog, then clones readable
 cloneable RAM and copies committed saves/storage under `<title data>/recovery`.
